WEBVTT

00:11.560 --> 00:12.980
Durability.

00:12.980 --> 00:13.980
Ease of wear.

00:13.980 --> 00:15.620
Protection.

00:15.620 --> 00:17.400
And beauty.

00:17.400 --> 00:20.570
A new style for the lady
adventurer of the future.

00:20.570 --> 00:21.310
Set out on an adventure
that's both stylish and safe.

00:21.310 --> 00:23.110
(Heal)
Set out on an adventure
that's both stylish and safe.

00:24.030 --> 00:27.460
Here to support you on every adventure:

00:30.600 --> 00:32.000
Earthys.

02:02.500 --> 02:06.010
(Morungen Underground Waterway)

02:09.760 --> 02:13.560
(Episode 5: Mission)

02:13.560 --> 02:15.770
(Episode 5: Mission)
Man, don't we have any better food?

02:15.770 --> 02:17.010
Man, don't we have any better food?

02:17.010 --> 02:18.920
When the chore boy was with us,

02:18.920 --> 02:22.390
we got to eat decent stuff
from that weird pot of his.

02:22.390 --> 02:25.280
Does it really help anyone
to keep griping about that?

02:26.110 --> 02:27.850
Are you guys all ready?

02:27.850 --> 02:30.910
Do you have your potions? How's your mana?

02:31.210 --> 02:35.040
Huh? I didn't bring any potions.

02:35.040 --> 02:37.410
What's the point when we've got Camilla?

02:37.410 --> 02:39.860
Don't depend on me for everything.

02:39.860 --> 02:42.040
Mana potions are expensive, you know.

02:42.450 --> 02:45.460
Hmph. You sure were sucking
them down before, though.

02:45.460 --> 02:46.540
That was—

02:46.540 --> 02:48.450
Okay, enough.

02:48.450 --> 02:50.300
We're up against Bogles this time.

02:50.730 --> 02:52.130
True.

02:52.130 --> 02:56.060
I could handle one measly Bogle on my own.

02:56.540 --> 02:59.310
Jamie, get us ready to
stream as fast as you can.

02:59.600 --> 03:01.320
Give me just a bit longer.

03:02.200 --> 03:05.420
You can barely use magic,
and you're weak as hell.

03:05.420 --> 03:08.070
At least get a little job like this right.

03:08.770 --> 03:12.490
If only Jamie could use
healing magic, too...

03:12.490 --> 03:14.570
But if she can't, that's that, I suppose.

03:15.620 --> 03:16.830
It's ready.

03:16.830 --> 03:18.840
All right, then, let's go.

03:18.840 --> 03:19.600
Yep.

03:27.640 --> 03:29.460
Another failure, eh?

03:30.100 --> 03:32.900
If your score continues to drop,

03:32.900 --> 03:35.970
there's a chance you may be demoted
to a lower adventurer rank.

03:37.290 --> 03:41.640
Simon Berkley, have you considered
accepting easier quests?

03:41.640 --> 03:42.860
What?!

03:42.860 --> 03:47.360
Let's see... Might I suggest
a C-rank quest next time?

03:47.640 --> 03:49.730
I'm an A-rank adventurer!

03:50.110 --> 03:53.860
And I'm saying you aren't producing
results worthy of one.

03:54.150 --> 03:57.120
That's not Thunder Pike's fault, though!

03:57.490 --> 03:59.800
You haven't introduced any new
members for us in a while,

03:59.800 --> 04:03.490
and this time, we faced not
only a Bogle, but a Named!

04:03.490 --> 04:04.620
We couldn't have known!

04:04.620 --> 04:08.310
Still, a failed quest is a failed quest.

04:08.310 --> 04:09.210
Forget it!

04:17.230 --> 04:20.130
Demote us? What does she take us for?!

04:20.130 --> 04:22.960
She only said there's a
chance it could happen.

04:22.960 --> 04:26.850
Point is, high-ranked quests might be too
much when there are only four of us.

04:27.240 --> 04:30.730
Then go find us a new member already.

04:31.050 --> 04:33.560
Isn't that your job as our leader?

04:35.770 --> 04:39.490
You know... maybe we should
just bring him back.

04:39.800 --> 04:44.000
I agree. He has made quite a
name for himself as a streamer.

04:44.450 --> 04:46.570
Didn't you say you two
were childhood pals,

04:46.570 --> 04:48.950
and that he was basically your minion?

04:48.950 --> 04:51.630
I need something that'll convince him.

04:51.630 --> 04:52.510
Like what?

04:52.870 --> 04:55.000
If we want to get him interested,

04:55.000 --> 04:56.880
we have to take on Achromatic Darkness.

04:58.490 --> 05:01.140
Achromatic Darkness? Why
do we need to go there?

05:01.710 --> 05:03.590
It's Yuke's dream.

05:03.590 --> 05:07.950
He always said he wanted to see the
end of the world, like some dumb kid.

05:07.950 --> 05:11.900
But if we do that, I bet he'll
jump on our invitation.

05:12.550 --> 05:16.770
So we should team up with some other
parties for a joint quest or something

05:16.770 --> 05:19.230
and take on Achromatic Darkness.

05:19.230 --> 05:20.910
Just pretending to will be enough.

05:21.570 --> 05:23.410
We don't have to take this seriously.

05:24.060 --> 05:28.600
A C-rank newbie party like that couldn't
even try it if they wanted to.

05:28.600 --> 05:31.720
That's a good idea!
He'll come crying then!

05:31.720 --> 05:32.800
Hey! Refill!

05:33.140 --> 05:33.920
Coming.

05:38.620 --> 05:40.050
Temporarily closed?

05:40.050 --> 05:40.810
Yeah.

05:41.500 --> 05:45.810
The Aion Ruins Dungeon is temporarily
closed for an investigation.

05:46.480 --> 05:51.580
A Shadow Stalker showed up there after
none had been seen in over ten years.

05:51.580 --> 05:53.070
It's to be expected.

05:53.390 --> 05:54.840
Are they from Earthys?

05:54.840 --> 05:56.320
Yeah, those girls!

05:56.320 --> 05:58.500
They're the real deal! So cute!

05:58.500 --> 05:59.700
I'm rooting for you!

05:59.700 --> 06:01.450
Hmph. They're just a bunch of newbies.

06:05.440 --> 06:07.520
Of course people are gonna be jealous.

06:07.520 --> 06:08.760
Don't let it get to you.

06:09.560 --> 06:11.710
Yeah. I'm okay.

06:12.340 --> 06:14.490
Right over here, folks.

06:14.490 --> 06:15.960
Oh, okay!

06:21.800 --> 06:24.350
There's plenty of storage space.

06:24.350 --> 06:25.850
Yeah. It's big.

06:26.300 --> 06:28.910
The interior is quite nice, as well.

06:28.910 --> 06:32.610
It offers easy access to the main
street, and it has a backyard, too.

06:33.090 --> 06:35.750
Hmm... We should pass on this one.

06:37.240 --> 06:39.980
One-story houses are easy targets
for burglary and raids,

06:39.980 --> 06:42.180
and it's hard to stop
people from looking in.

06:42.180 --> 06:45.240
Not what you want for a
house full of women.

06:45.240 --> 06:46.850
That makes sense.

06:49.620 --> 06:54.500
This is an apartment that's been
renovated into a family home.

06:54.990 --> 06:57.000
The first floor is a shared space,

06:57.000 --> 07:00.510
and there are private bedrooms
on the second floor.

07:00.510 --> 07:03.000
This place looks pretty good.

07:03.000 --> 07:07.520
It has underground storage,
and you can go up on the roof, too.

07:07.520 --> 07:10.310
That'll be good for drying our laundry.

07:10.310 --> 07:12.650
I like this one more than the last one!

07:13.330 --> 07:14.190
Yeah.

07:14.190 --> 07:17.320
Mr. Monday, can we put a hold on this one?

07:17.890 --> 07:19.840
But of course.

07:19.840 --> 07:22.820
Now, allow me to show you
one last property.

07:25.200 --> 07:26.830
This is the place.

07:31.400 --> 07:32.840
What is it?

07:32.840 --> 07:35.590
Thunder Pike's base is near here.

07:36.110 --> 07:38.460
It is? Then...

07:38.900 --> 07:43.070
Mr. Monday, I'm sorry, but we don't
need to see the next property.

07:43.070 --> 07:44.470
Oh, is that so?

07:44.920 --> 07:47.790
Well, then... what would you like to do?

07:47.790 --> 07:50.160
I like that last place we saw.

07:50.160 --> 07:51.010
Me, too.

07:51.010 --> 07:52.100
I agree.

07:52.640 --> 07:55.100
You're sure you don't want
to see the next one?

07:55.630 --> 07:59.230
I don't want to have them as neighbors.

07:59.230 --> 08:02.220
You don't want to see them either, do you?

08:02.220 --> 08:02.820
Right...

08:03.510 --> 08:06.200
Okay, so that's the house we're getting!

08:09.060 --> 08:12.420
Okay, I think that's everyone's stuff.

08:12.420 --> 08:13.870
Let's take it all up to the rooms.

08:14.280 --> 08:15.590
Do we know who gets which room?

08:15.590 --> 08:16.840
No, not yet.

08:16.840 --> 08:18.250
We were just about to decide.

08:18.250 --> 08:21.080
Which room would you like, Master?

08:21.080 --> 08:21.880
Huh?

08:23.060 --> 08:26.260
If you'd like the one at the
end or the nearest one...

08:26.740 --> 08:28.870
We'd like to hear your preferences.

08:28.870 --> 08:30.260
What are you talking about?

08:30.540 --> 08:32.640
I'm talking about your room.

08:33.230 --> 08:36.910
Um... Just so I'm clear here...

08:36.910 --> 08:39.520
You aren't talking about me
living here with you, are you?

08:39.520 --> 08:42.530
That's exactly
what I'm talking about, yes.

08:42.940 --> 08:43.900
With you?

08:44.340 --> 08:45.530
With us.

08:45.530 --> 08:47.370
It's our party's base, after all!

08:47.790 --> 08:48.740
Yeah.

08:50.200 --> 08:53.120
But... I can't do that. I'm a man.

08:53.460 --> 08:56.750
But when we camp out,
you sleep right beside us anyway!

08:56.750 --> 08:58.130
But that's not the—

08:58.130 --> 08:59.560
It is the same!

08:59.560 --> 09:02.450
We trust you, Yuke.

09:02.450 --> 09:06.510
And getting to eat your cooking
every day would be awesome!

09:07.000 --> 09:10.080
Marina, we'll all do
the chores in rotation.

09:11.550 --> 09:13.140
But still...

09:13.140 --> 09:15.110
You might as well give up.

09:15.920 --> 09:19.650
Besides, you're the one who said it was
dangerous for a household to be all women.

09:21.170 --> 09:22.400
Fine, fine.

09:22.920 --> 09:26.490
Everyone make sure to
keep your doors locked.

09:26.820 --> 09:30.260
Keep the fact that I'm a man
in the back of your mind

09:30.260 --> 09:32.120
so we keep the risk
of trouble to a minimum.

09:32.440 --> 09:33.530
Okay!

09:33.530 --> 09:34.750
Understood!

09:34.750 --> 09:35.370
Got it.

09:36.010 --> 09:37.860
Okay, then...

09:37.860 --> 09:40.000
Let's finish moving in.

09:46.350 --> 09:48.760
A gift from me to celebrate the move.

09:48.760 --> 09:50.010
A tablet!

09:50.010 --> 09:52.200
Wow! It's huge!

09:52.200 --> 09:53.760
Wasn't this expensive?

09:54.090 --> 09:59.420
I figured we'd want to watch logs and
conquest streams here to work out strategies,

09:59.420 --> 10:00.990
so I splurged a bit.

10:00.990 --> 10:02.620
Thanks, Yuke!

10:02.620 --> 10:04.530
Thank you, Master!

10:05.020 --> 10:07.150
Thank you. Let's toast.

10:08.920 --> 10:10.530
Yeah, you're right.

10:10.830 --> 10:14.830
Then, as our leader, why don't
you lead us in a toast?

10:15.320 --> 10:19.590
In that case... to our new life,
and to the future of Clover!

10:19.590 --> 10:20.460
Cheers!

10:20.920 --> 10:22.210
Cheers!

10:31.410 --> 10:32.830
What's up, Rain?

10:34.100 --> 10:34.600
(Mission)

10:34.600 --> 10:36.100
(Mission)
Mission:

10:36.100 --> 10:36.880
(Achromatic Darkness)

10:36.880 --> 10:38.600
(Achromatic Darkness)
Achromatic Darkness.

10:39.520 --> 10:41.230
Achromatic Darkness...

10:42.740 --> 10:43.560
Meow!

10:43.560 --> 10:46.760
Today, in response to multiple petitions,
the kingdom has granted permission

10:46.760 --> 10:49.240
to conduct an investigation
on Achromatic Darkness,

10:49.240 --> 10:51.290
the dungeon that had been locked down!

10:51.290 --> 10:53.310
It will be led by Thunder Pike,

10:53.310 --> 10:55.400
and the goal will be
reaching the Abyss Gate.

10:55.400 --> 10:58.290
This will be a large-scale
investigation quest!

11:03.640 --> 11:04.630
Yuke.

11:06.300 --> 11:08.010
Um... Master...

11:08.510 --> 11:10.650
Yeah. Don't worry.

11:10.650 --> 11:13.510
It's not like there's a
race to get there.

11:13.960 --> 11:17.060
It's true that taking on Achromatic
Darkness is my dream,

11:17.560 --> 11:21.040
but the details of my dream
have changed a bit.

11:21.040 --> 11:22.100
They have?

11:22.590 --> 11:26.480
We promised we'd all go to the
Abyss Gate together, didn't we?

11:27.000 --> 11:29.490
And weren't we going to livestream it?

11:29.490 --> 11:30.150
Yeah!

11:30.460 --> 11:33.160
So you don't need to worry about a thing.

11:33.160 --> 11:34.160
Okay.

11:34.430 --> 11:35.420
Sure.

11:35.420 --> 11:37.660
Okay, why don't we have another toast?

11:37.660 --> 11:39.190
Yeah, let's!

11:39.190 --> 11:40.290
Let's drink up!

11:43.140 --> 11:44.620
A Mail Bird?

11:45.440 --> 11:46.920
From the guild?

11:48.610 --> 11:50.170
A request to spot?

11:50.170 --> 11:51.330
For me?

11:51.330 --> 11:56.340
Yes, and they said they wanted
a reply as soon as possible.

11:56.340 --> 11:58.930
And the ones who want you to spot are...

12:01.680 --> 12:02.548
(Request for: Yuke Feldio
Quest Description: Temporarily join the party)

12:02.549 --> 12:03.495
(Time Frame: Until the Achromatic Darkness
investigation mission is complete)

12:03.496 --> 12:04.828
(Points of Note: Due to the registration
time limit set by the kingdom,
a reply is needed as soon as possible.)

12:04.829 --> 12:06.010
(Upon quest completion, the appointed individual
may be named an official party member.)

12:06.011 --> 12:06.690
(Posted by: Thunder Pike)

12:06.690 --> 12:08.440
Thunder Pike...

12:09.360 --> 12:13.350
Okay, could you tell them
that I respectfully decline?

12:13.350 --> 12:14.700
I thought as much.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.900
Yuke, look.

12:22.890 --> 12:24.940
Oh, right.

12:24.940 --> 12:27.960
He has way more drive to take
action than most people.

12:27.960 --> 12:30.210
What is the meaning of this?!

12:30.210 --> 12:33.340
No special meaning.
It's just what it says.

12:33.720 --> 12:35.570
It's Achromatic Darkness!

12:35.570 --> 12:36.870
Isn't that what you want?!

12:36.870 --> 12:37.970
Why did you refuse?!

12:38.510 --> 12:42.350
As you can imagine, I was surprised
that you remembered my dream.

12:42.640 --> 12:44.080
Of course I do!

12:44.080 --> 12:46.600
We've been friends since we were kids!

12:47.600 --> 12:51.900
I'm proud of the fact that my
former party is going into

12:51.900 --> 12:53.780
the toughest dungeon in the kingdom.

12:53.780 --> 12:55.360
Best of luck to you.

12:55.360 --> 12:56.990
Don't talk like this doesn't concern you!

12:57.640 --> 13:00.990
We've already been making plans
based on you being there!

13:01.460 --> 13:03.050
Well, I'm not going.

13:03.050 --> 13:05.120
Not with Thunder Pike, at least.

13:05.420 --> 13:07.690
Stop this already, Yuke!

13:07.690 --> 13:09.880
You're the one who needs to stop, Simon!

13:10.190 --> 13:12.460
If you'd think for one second,
you'd get it!

13:12.460 --> 13:16.480
Sending a spot request to someone
who's in an active party

13:16.480 --> 13:18.140
is the same as unwanted solicitation!

13:18.140 --> 13:20.050
It's a major breach of etiquette!

13:21.230 --> 13:24.630
So long as it's just a request,
I have the right to refuse.

13:24.630 --> 13:25.480
Besides—

13:25.480 --> 13:26.140
Shut up!

13:27.140 --> 13:29.400
You're the one who up and left us!

13:29.400 --> 13:31.480
You've put us through so much trouble!

13:31.480 --> 13:36.150
And I arranged an investigation quest
in Achromatic Darkness just for you!

13:37.930 --> 13:41.580
Don't talk about my leaving as
if it were totally one-sided.

13:41.950 --> 13:42.870
Excuse me?!

13:43.230 --> 13:46.120
Adventure prep, quest research,

13:46.120 --> 13:48.830
intel-gathering for dungeon conquests...

13:48.830 --> 13:51.860
You dumped everything that
didn't involve combat on me!

13:51.860 --> 13:53.800
Must've made things pretty
damn easy for you, huh?

13:54.440 --> 13:58.910
Day after day, I sucked it up and kept at it,
believing you'd understand someday.

13:58.910 --> 14:01.050
You guys are the ones who betrayed that!

14:01.560 --> 14:03.180
Don't act like we're buddies now!

14:07.830 --> 14:09.350
I'm okay. Sorry.

14:10.600 --> 14:14.840
L-Listen, Yuke... If that's
how you feel, then come back.

14:14.840 --> 14:17.520
We're comrades chasing the
same dream, aren't we?

14:17.520 --> 14:19.300
It'll work out this time!

14:19.300 --> 14:20.610
It's too late.

14:20.610 --> 14:22.490
My comrades are the members of Clover.

14:22.810 --> 14:24.370
Not Thunder Pike.

14:28.400 --> 14:30.850
What's gonna happen to us, then?!

14:30.850 --> 14:32.620
We can't fail again!

14:32.620 --> 14:36.260
If this keeps up, our rank will
drop, and we'll be ruined!

14:36.590 --> 14:38.720
What you guys do is none of my concern.

14:39.800 --> 14:40.720
Let's go, Rain.

14:44.560 --> 14:46.960
If that's how you're gonna be,
then forget it!

14:46.960 --> 14:49.660
I've got some ideas of my own, you know!

14:54.610 --> 14:55.760
(Two Weeks Later)

14:55.760 --> 14:56.610
(Two Weeks Later)
What?

14:57.230 --> 15:00.360
It's very likely that an
Overflow is occurring.

15:01.170 --> 15:06.240
In addition to what you reported
at Aion, it's also here and here.

15:06.820 --> 15:10.330
Abnormalities have been
observed over here, too.

15:10.330 --> 15:12.040
Are you going to make me say it again?

15:13.450 --> 15:15.840
We may be looking at a Stampede.

15:16.950 --> 15:21.160
If weird things are happening in
multiple dungeons, then yeah, maybe.

15:21.720 --> 15:23.340
What did the Royal Academy say?

15:23.790 --> 15:27.600
That they can't deny the possibility.

15:27.600 --> 15:32.440
Hang on... So the quest to
investigate Achromatic Darkness...

15:32.440 --> 15:34.810
The fact that they granted
permission so easily

15:34.810 --> 15:37.610
is probably connected to
a Stampede investigation.

15:37.610 --> 15:38.480
I get it.

15:39.510 --> 15:44.620
Yuke, I want to put out a nomination
quest for you—no, for Clover.

15:46.650 --> 15:49.000
An investigation quest
in Achromatic Darkness.

15:49.000 --> 15:53.250
Don't send a C-rank party on a job
you know they can't handle, Benwood.

15:53.250 --> 15:57.380
There are other A-rank parties in this
besides Thunder Pike, aren't there?

15:57.800 --> 16:03.130
Scordia has already gotten fed up with
Thunder Pike and Grant's Blow, and backed out.

16:04.690 --> 16:06.940
They can't be trusted.

16:06.940 --> 16:12.660
Not a single one of them even
submitted a formal application.

16:14.040 --> 16:15.680
You've read this, haven't you?

16:16.220 --> 16:18.770
To me, this is a piece of treasure.

16:19.190 --> 16:22.870
The one and only conquest log that
exists for Achromatic Darkness...

16:23.790 --> 16:26.160
The official record proving
the Abyss Gate's existence.

16:26.720 --> 16:29.310
And that's why I want you to do this.

16:29.310 --> 16:32.290
I'm not asking you to conquer it.
Just investigate it.

16:32.290 --> 16:35.950
But I'd have to conquer it in
order to progress through it.

16:35.950 --> 16:37.040
It's too dangerous.

16:37.420 --> 16:40.390
Flexibility is a must in that dungeon.

16:40.390 --> 16:43.790
I need someone like you,
who can do just about anything.

16:43.790 --> 16:47.320
Not to mention... you can use this.

16:47.320 --> 16:48.300
That's...

16:48.840 --> 16:51.060
A Scroll of Exit.

16:51.370 --> 16:52.700
It's all yours.

16:53.180 --> 16:55.380
You're giving me something this valuable?

16:55.380 --> 16:56.310
Why go so far?

16:56.880 --> 17:00.120
I want information confirmed
by your two eyes.

17:00.120 --> 17:03.000
If I could, I'd go myself,

17:03.000 --> 17:06.320
but given my position,
I can't leave my seat.

17:06.320 --> 17:10.330
The most crucial thing here is getting
a report from a source I can trust.

17:12.350 --> 17:13.580
Come in.

17:14.110 --> 17:15.360
Pardon me.

17:17.090 --> 17:19.810
Here you go, Yuke.

17:20.710 --> 17:21.230
(Nomination Quest, Quest Type: Mission,
Request for: The party Clover)

17:21.230 --> 17:23.100
(Nomination Quest, Quest Type: Mission,
Request for: The party Clover)
"Mission: investigate and report
on Achromatic Darkness.

17:23.100 --> 17:25.180
(Quest Description: Investigate and report
on Achromatic Darkness, Time Limit: None)
"Mission: investigate and report
on Achromatic Darkness.

17:25.180 --> 17:25.720
(Points of Note: The party involved will be granted
provisional A-rank status during the mission.)

17:25.720 --> 17:25.970
(Points of Note: The party involved will be granted
provisional A-rank status during the mission.)
The party involved will be granted
provisional A-rank status during the mission.

17:25.970 --> 17:28.330
(Points of Note: The party involved will be
granted provisional A-rank status during the mission.)
The party involved will be granted
provisional A-rank status during the mission.

17:28.330 --> 17:30.180
(Posted by: Vincent V, King of Welmelia)
The party involved will be granted
provisional A-rank status during the mission.

17:30.180 --> 17:30.720
(Posted by: Vincent V, King of Welmelia)

17:30.990 --> 17:33.620
Posted by the King of Welmelia."

17:35.070 --> 17:37.520
I suddenly feel like a huge deal.

17:37.520 --> 17:39.110
All right. I understand.

17:39.110 --> 17:40.980
I'll discuss it with my partymates.

17:41.560 --> 17:43.070
Please do, Yuke.

17:49.560 --> 17:50.740
I was thinking...

17:51.330 --> 17:52.370
and I'd like to refuse.

17:52.370 --> 17:54.760
What? You're turning them down?

17:54.760 --> 17:56.160
But why?

17:56.160 --> 17:58.380
I can't complain about the reward,

17:58.380 --> 18:00.630
and I'm sure the payoff in
our scores would be huge.

18:01.410 --> 18:03.860
But we're lacking in
preparation and experience.

18:04.360 --> 18:08.260
There's too much we still need before
we can take on Achromatic Darkness.

18:08.260 --> 18:12.620
Master, our experience aside,
I think we can make preparations.

18:12.620 --> 18:14.890
Luckily for us, we have the latest armor.

18:15.890 --> 18:19.920
This is an opportunity for us, too.

18:19.920 --> 18:25.000
We're going to traverse this dungeon
and search for the Abyss Gate one day.

18:25.000 --> 18:28.400
We should consider this a
good chance to scout it out.

18:28.690 --> 18:29.910
Silk...

18:30.310 --> 18:31.590
She's right!

18:31.590 --> 18:36.430
If we don't, that lack of experience you
just brought up will stay with us forever!

18:36.430 --> 18:38.230
But the thing is, Marina...

18:38.230 --> 18:39.540
You're scared.

18:40.050 --> 18:41.100
Scared?

18:41.790 --> 18:44.800
Is that it? Am I scared?

18:44.800 --> 18:45.930
Yuke?

18:45.930 --> 18:47.300
Master?

18:47.800 --> 18:50.300
Are you afraid of losing us?

18:52.880 --> 18:54.600
Yeah. I am.

18:54.600 --> 18:57.040
I would hate that more than anything.

18:57.630 --> 18:58.640
It scares me.

19:01.150 --> 19:02.190
Rain...

19:02.590 --> 19:05.320
Yeah. We feel the same way.

19:10.140 --> 19:12.280
Yuke... Let's go for it.

19:12.280 --> 19:13.240
But...

19:13.820 --> 19:17.020
Do you trust us that little?

19:17.020 --> 19:18.770
That's not it.

19:18.770 --> 19:20.710
I think you're the best
partymates I could have.

19:20.710 --> 19:23.080
Then you have to move
ahead toward your dream.

19:24.210 --> 19:25.930
That's right, Yuke!

19:25.930 --> 19:26.590
Yes.

19:30.270 --> 19:33.400
Come on, Yuke, let's get
ready for adventuring!

19:33.400 --> 19:35.220
Let me know what we need!

19:35.790 --> 19:39.270
Let's form a battle plan
based on our previous streams.

19:39.660 --> 19:40.670
You guys...

19:41.470 --> 19:43.690
I was wrong. Sorry.

19:43.690 --> 19:45.120
No kidding!

19:45.120 --> 19:49.440
I mean, you wouldn't have brought this
to us if you weren't interested, right?

19:50.390 --> 19:52.800
Marina, don't bring that up.

19:52.800 --> 19:54.270
I was holding it in.

19:55.030 --> 19:57.240
Don't blame Master.

19:57.240 --> 20:02.190
He thought all this through and
prioritized our safety in the end.

20:02.190 --> 20:06.420
We need to be dependable enough
that we don't worry him.

20:06.420 --> 20:08.360
Yeah, I agree!

20:08.360 --> 20:10.800
So don't worry about it, Yuke!

20:11.150 --> 20:12.790
I get it now.

20:12.790 --> 20:15.640
I wanted to go there with all of you.

20:15.640 --> 20:18.680
Let go to Achromatic Darkness as Clover!

20:19.130 --> 20:20.060
Yeah.

20:20.060 --> 20:21.000
Yes!

20:21.000 --> 20:22.000
Let's go!

20:25.660 --> 20:28.320
We'll be accepting that mission.

20:28.620 --> 20:31.690
I'm sorry if this seems like I'm
taking advantage of your dream.

20:31.690 --> 20:34.950
It sure does, but I'm grateful.

20:35.420 --> 20:37.950
Anyway, I talked it over with these three,

20:37.950 --> 20:41.590
and we want to solicit a spot
to improve our chances.

20:41.590 --> 20:44.000
Could you introduce a good Scout?

20:44.000 --> 20:47.000
Mamar expected you to ask that.

20:48.010 --> 20:51.260
This is Nene, and she's
interested in being your spot.

20:52.890 --> 20:53.960
Nene?

20:54.420 --> 20:56.230
She has a tail!

20:56.230 --> 20:57.180
And cat ears...

20:57.520 --> 20:59.150
She's a friend's daughter.

20:59.150 --> 21:01.790
She took a joke a bit
too far in her homeland,

21:02.270 --> 21:05.440
so I took her in and helped
her turn things around.

21:05.440 --> 21:07.310
Well, how about that...

21:07.310 --> 21:09.460
Nene, introduce yourself.

21:11.600 --> 21:13.520
I'm Nene Shilfindle.

21:13.520 --> 21:13.690
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

21:13.690 --> 21:15.190
(Ferci Nene)
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

21:15.190 --> 21:15.200
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

21:15.200 --> 21:15.900
(Thief)
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

21:15.900 --> 21:16.720
(Ninja)
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

21:16.720 --> 21:17.570
(Ninja)
I'm rank C!

21:17.570 --> 21:18.450
(Score: Rank C)
I'm rank C!

21:18.450 --> 21:20.980
I'll devote my whole body
and soul to this job!

21:21.530 --> 21:23.580
I promise I'll be useful,

21:23.980 --> 21:25.960
so please hire me!

22:55.960 --> 22:56.760
(Achromatic Darkness)

22:56.760 --> 22:59.100
(Achromatic Darkness)
Next time, "Achromatic Darkness."

22:59.100 --> 23:00.970
(Achromatic Darkness)
